A||N||4||Verticalspeed||V8 W/ Edelbrock Carb Questions||||1||
Z||000000||Verticalspeed||04-22-2001||07:38 PM||||Is any one on this group using a 600 CFM Edelrbock carb with a v8 setup? I am curious to know what size jets and rods you have used to fine tune it, based on your elevation. Did you bolt it on out of the box?||||reg||1
Z||000001||BBBAD GT||04-23-2001||09:08 AM||||I just bought a new 600 Edelbrock, and haven't touched the jets/rods yet.  Its runs fine, but I could probably go a little lean on the cruise/WOT, but haven't had time yet to mess with it.  You do have to play with the idle adjustments.  <P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">        <P><A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/V8Specs.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8 For Sale</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Butter||04-23-2001||11:07 AM||||I use a 650 eldelbrock and bolted it on from the box.  I don't like the vacuum secondaries.  Don't perform well with lateral g's.  Also has a bad habit of loading up gas upon a warm shutoff and a soon restart.||||reg||12
Z||000003||Archie||04-23-2001||12:43 PM||||I thought we had answered that question for you back in this thread.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007306.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007306.html</A> <P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000004||Verticalspeed||04-25-2001||03:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B>I thought we had answered that question for you back in this thread.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007306.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007306.html</A> <P>Archie</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I thought I mentioned that the local shops here don't know SH*** about anything!<BR>I have been looking for a buddy who installed a 600cmf in his h.p. camaro to see what he did for jets and rods...the thing that puzzles me is...how do you know that the thing is set up right and how do you tell that you are getting the engine's ideal output?<P>||||reg||1
